  "task_text": " Supplemental Diagnostic\n4 XP\nMathematical Foundations II: Supplemental Diagnostic Exam\nCompleted @ 8:22 PM\n1.Determining the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of Multiple Transformations\n?\n\nThe triangle shown above is transformed subsequently by functions \n𝑓\n1\n(\n𝑥\n,\n𝑦\n)\n↦\n(\n𝑥\n−\n2\n,\n𝑦\n)\n and \n𝑓\n2\n(\n𝑥\n,\n𝑦\n)\n↦\n(\n−\n𝑥\n,\n𝑦\n)\n.\n What is the resulting triangle?\n\nMThu, Apr 2nd @ 8:20 PM|Elapsed: 1:59\nCorrect\n2.Identifying Properties of Platonic Solids\n?\n\nWhich of the following statements must be true regarding any tetrahedron?\n\nIt has \n4\n congruent faces, each in the form of a right triangle\nExactly \n3\n faces meet at each vertex\nIt has \n4\n edges\nMThu, Apr 2nd @ 8:21 PM|Elapsed: 0:14\nIncorrect\n3.Calculating an Unknown Angle Given an Angle Bisector and Two Angle Measurements\n?\n\nIn the figure above, \n\t\n𝑂\n𝐷\n→\n is the bisector of \n∠\n𝐴\n𝑂\n𝐶\n.\n If \n𝑚\n∠\n𝐵\n𝑂\n𝐴\n=\n80\n∘\n and \n𝑚\n∠\n𝐵\n𝑂\n𝐶\n=\n22\n∘\n,\n find \n𝑚\n∠\n𝐷\n𝑂\n𝐶\n.\n\nEThu, Apr 2nd @ 8:22 PM|Elapsed: 0:36\nCorrect",
